$comfy — run a ComfyUI API workflow (exported JSON) on a live Comfy server

SUMMARY
  Loads a workflow JSON exported from ComfyUI (API format), replaces INPUT_*
  placeholder strings with data from the Anthill bundle, queues the graph on a
  running ComfyUI server via HTTP, waits for completion, and downloads outputs
  into images[] / videos[] / sounds[] / files[].

  Anthill does not embed ComfyUI. Comfy must already be running (desktop or
  python main.py --listen). Each $comfy invocation queues one Comfy /prompt job
  per input image when the workflow uses INPUT_IMAGE / INPUT_IMAGE.png; extra
  images in images[] do not batch in a single job.

SYNTAX
  $comfy(port=8000, json='Qwen-Rapid-AIO_4.json')
  $comfy(json='Rapid-AIO-Mega__3_exp.json')
  $comfy(port=8188, json='comfy_workflows/my_graph.json')

  Parallel — same inputs, different workflows or prompts:
    ( $comfy(port=8000, json='a.json'), $comfy(port=8000, json='b.json') )

  Sequence with @ refs for separate prompts:
    @realistic: @images -> (
      @style_prompt -> $comfy(port=8000, json='Qwen-Rapid-AIO_4.json'),
      @motion_prompt -> $comfy(port=8000, json='Rapid-AIO-Mega__3_exp.json')
    )

HOW TO ADD A NEW WORKFLOW (from ComfyUI)

  1. Build and test the graph in ComfyUI until it runs correctly in the UI.

  2. Export API-format JSON (required — not the UI workflow save):
       - Menu: Save (API Format) or Export (API Format)
       - Or enable Dev mode → Save (API Format)
     The file must be a flat object keyed by node id strings, each node having
     class_type and inputs — not the visual graph with nodes/links positions.

  3. Insert placeholders in node inputs (any string value in the JSON):
       - LoadImage "image": "INPUT_IMAGE" or "INPUT_IMAGE.png"
       - Text / CLIP / Qwen encode nodes: "INPUT_PROMPT"
       - LoadAudio or similar: "INPUT_SOUND" (see INPUT_SOUND below)
       - KSampler / seed widgets: "INPUT_SEED" (random int 1–200000000 per job)
     Use the exact token text; Anthill does substring replacement in all strings.

  4. Save the file into the project:
       comfy_workflows/MyWorkflow.json
     Recommended naming: short, no spaces (e.g. Qwen-Rapid-AIO_4.json).

  5. Reference it in .ah:
       $comfy(port=8000, json='MyWorkflow.json')
     json= is looked up without a folder prefix if the file is under
     comfy_workflows/.

  6. Start ComfyUI on the same port you pass (or set COMFYUI_URL):
       cd path/to/ComfyUI
       python main.py --listen 127.0.0.1 --port 8000

  7. Run Anthill with inputs in the bundle (see INPUT below).

  Tip: After a run, inspect sessions/.../N__comfy/patched_workflow.json to see
  the exact JSON sent to Comfy. Fix placeholders there if a node was missed.

WORKFLOW JSON SEARCH PATH (json= argument)

  Resolved in order until found:
    - Absolute path
    - Relative to session base_dir
    - ./<file>
    - <repo>/<file>
    - <repo>/comfy_workflows/<file>   ← preferred location
    - ./comfy_workflows/<file>
    - <repo>/workflows/<file>
    - <repo>/comfy/<file>

PLACEHOLDERS (replace in the exported JSON before running)

  INPUT_IMAGE.png / INPUT_IMAGE
    Replaced with the filename Comfy returns after uploading each image in
    images[] (one Comfy /prompt job per file when the workflow uses this
    placeholder). Both tokens get the same name. Use either form in LoadImage.

  INPUT_PROMPT
    Replaced with joined prompts[] link text and/or the instruction body
    under the $comfy step (merged before the call when using @ref -> $comfy).

  INPUT_SOUND
    Replaced with a filename copied into Comfy's input folder. Set env:
    COMFYUI_INPUT_DIR=G:/path/to/ComfyUI/input
    (Comfy has no /upload/audio API; file is copied there before the run.)

  INPUT_SEED
    Replaced with a random integer from 1 to 200000000 (new value each Comfy
    /prompt job). Use a scalar widget value in the JSON, e.g.
    "seed": "INPUT_SEED" → "seed": 12345678.
    Do not use ["INPUT_SEED", 0] in new workflows — Comfy treats [N, 0] as a
    link to node N; Anthill still fixes that legacy form to a scalar int.

INPUT

  images[]  — required if the JSON contains INPUT_IMAGE or INPUT_IMAGE.png
  sounds[]  — required if the JSON contains INPUT_SOUND
  prompts[] — used for INPUT_PROMPT; one Comfy job per prompt link (not joined).
    Multiple prompts × multiple images = one job per (image, prompt) pair.
  Instruction body on the same @ line as $comfy — merged into INPUT_PROMPT
    when the pipeline is @ref -> $comfy (not when $comfy is first in the chain).

  Typical pipeline:
    @images: @prompt -> $image(...)
    start frame in images[]
    @run: @images -> @my_prompt -> $comfy(json='MyWorkflow.json')
    style / motion text for INPUT_PROMPT

OUTPUT

  Downloads from Comfy history into the session op folder, then appends links:
    .png / .jpg / .webp  → images[]
    .mp4 / .webm         → videos[]
    .wav / .mp3          → sounds[]
    other                → files[]

  Multiple SaveImage / video nodes → multiple links in the matching arrays.

ARGUMENTS

  port=   — Comfy listen port (default 8188). Builds http://127.0.0.1:PORT.
            Must match the port ComfyUI was started with.
  json=   — Workflow filename or path (see WORKFLOW JSON SEARCH PATH).
  workflow= — alias for json=

BEHAVIOR

  - One $comfy invocation = one POST /upload/image (if needed) + one POST /prompt
    + poll /history until done + download outputs.
  - Parallel branches ( ... , ... ) each run a separate $comfy with the same
    incoming bundle (same image; prompts depend on @ref wiring per branch).
  - $comfy(...)[n] repeat syntax is not implemented; use parallel duplicate
    $comfy lines or run the instruction multiple times.
  - Prompt-consuming: prompts[] cleared after $comfy returns (like $image).
    Use a separate @instruction for text needed after $image if prompts were
    consumed upstream.

ENVIRONMENT

  COMFYUI_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
    Used when port= is omitted on $comfy.

  COMFYUI_INPUT_DIR=G:/ComfyUI/input
    Required for INPUT_SOUND placeholders.

  AH_EMULATE_COMFY=1
    Skip Comfy server; write stub texts (no GPU, for pipeline debugging).

DEPENDENCIES

  None in the Anthill orchestrator venv. ComfyUI runs in its own install with
  its own models and custom nodes matching the exported workflow.

SETUP CHECKLIST

  [ ] ComfyUI running and reachable (browser http://127.0.0.1:PORT)
  [ ] Workflow exported as API JSON, not UI JSON
  [ ] Placeholders edited in JSON
  [ ] File in comfy_workflows/
  [ ] Custom nodes used by the graph installed in ComfyUI
  [ ] Models/checkpoints paths valid in Comfy (same as when you tested in UI)
  [ ] port= matches Comfy --port

TROUBLESHOOTING

  Connection refused
    ComfyUI not running or wrong port / COMFYUI_URL.

  HTTP 500 on /upload/image
    Comfy running but rejected the file — use a real PNG from $image, not an
    empty placeholder; check Comfy console for traceback.

  Workflow error in history
    Missing custom node, wrong model path, or invalid patched JSON — compare
    patched_workflow.json with a manual test in Comfy.

  INPUT_PROMPT empty / wrong
    prompts[] cleared by earlier $image; add @prompt instruction before $comfy
    (see example_comfy.ah @realistic_image_prompt pattern).

  json file not found
    Put JSON under comfy_workflows/ or pass a full path in json=.

EXAMPLES

  Single workflow:
    @out: @images -> @caption -> $comfy(port=8000, json='Qwen-Rapid-AIO_4.json')
    make this image in the realistic style

  Two workflows, same image, different prompts (parallel):
    @realistic: @images -> (
      @realistic_image_prompt -> $comfy(port=8000, json='Qwen-Rapid-AIO_4.json'),
      @video_prompt -> $comfy(port=8000, json='Rapid-AIO-Mega__3_exp.json')
    )

  See example_comfy.ah in the repo root.

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes — prompts[] cleared after the external returns.
